## 🔒 TASK 1: Implement S3 Encryption Enforcement (via Terraform)

### ✅ Objective:
Enforce server-side encryption with KMS on all user profile objects uploaded to S3.

### ✅ Implementation Plan:

```hcl
# modules/s3-user-profiles/main.tf

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "user_profiles" {
  bucket = "user-profiles-bucket-${var.environment}"

  # Enable SSE-KMS by default
  encryption {
    sse_kms_enabled = true
  }

  # Block unencrypted uploads via bucket policy
  bucket_policy = data.aws_iam_policy_document.s3_encryption_policy.document
}

# Data source: Generate bucket policy enforcing encryption
data "aws_iam_policy_document" "s3_encryption_policy" {
  statement {
    effect    = "Deny"
    principal = "*"
    action    = "s3:PutObject"
    resource  = "${aws_s3_bucket.user_profiles.arn}/*"

    condition {
      test     = "Null"
      variable = "s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption"
      values   = ["true"]
    }
  }
}
```

### ✅ Key Security Controls Enforced:
| Control | Implemented? | How |
|-------|--------------|-----|
| SSE-KMS enabled per-object | ✅ | `encryption { sse_kms_enabled = true }` |
| Deny unencrypted PUTs | ✅ | Bucket policy with `Null` condition on `x-amz-server-side-encryption` |
| KMS key managed securely | ⚠️ *Pending* | Must ensure KMS key is customer-managed (CMK), not AWS-owned. |

> 💡 **Action Item (for junior dev):**  
> Ensure the KMS key used is **customer-managed**, created via `aws_kms_key`, with proper key policy allowing only the S3 service and required roles (e.g., Lambda/EC2) to use it.

